{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0002": "$f^{-1}(V)$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to S \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:af03a6583a8fa536ce4754ce900d4a5eb76497a2167221a93089851a8439a624", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82506046dd4effc141fdf586703798f52c5e62b0b8bf833759d1f46b75b05d4a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine open. Then <MATH_0002> is an open subscheme\nof the affine scheme <MATH_0003>, hence quasi-affine if and only if it is\nquasi-compact. This proves the first assertion. The quasi-compactness of any\n<MATH_0004> where <MATH_0005> is affine and <MATH_0006> quasi-separated follows from\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>\napplied to <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3e0bdf6b07a08feeac03c6e370e79a0b1367b142c0ff5787ce9f77c0b5ffdf6", "unit_id": "tag:01SP:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$g$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-affine-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9302385c95b5e665f210801395fa393b695bf72ffa460951ec7fba0ecd4eb659", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e6183a8828a4c2cb5e8fb043df227fdc09b9188c36ecfe92cbd9dfefc598e1c7", "source_text": "Suppose <MATH_0001> is a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is quasi-affine over <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> is quasi-separated over <MATH_0006>,\nthen <MATH_0007> is quasi-affine. In particular, any morphism from a\nquasi-affine scheme to a quasi-separated scheme is quasi-affine.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8b7b610fe88873a5646516f5aa5ef94bc121a408121577349c429c2fd09218ce", "unit_id": "tag:054G:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01SJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\times_S Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to X \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0003": "$Y \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-quasi-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-section-immersion}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-immersion-quasi-affine}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-composition-quasi-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3f91dae0765afc9f4259cda977ffaa54d8a59a31a97a46c46a0376be96e832d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:19a0161afa99c5a7be62690cc847dadf1e1e29ef7ed91f879c41e0d2d7807282", "source_text": "The base change <MATH_0001> is quasi-affine by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe morphism <MATH_0002> is\na quasi-compact immersion as <MATH_0003> is quasi-separated, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nA quasi-compact immersion is quasi-affine by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nand the composition of quasi-affine morphisms is quasi-affine\n(see Lemma <REF_0004>). Thus we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ac9823c86bfa6dbccd3b5a00ea0266287fc037a98e7f7b9ef8df91a468f68b5b", "unit_id": "tag:054G:proof"}
